 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Six hundred thousand people lost power overnight. Was the energy truce ever real?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Ukraine says Russia fired 39 ballistic missiles and over 120 drones at energy sites in Kyiv and Kharkiv. The prime minister says all three of Kyiv's heat and power plants were hit. City officials report at least three dead."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Zelenskyy calls it ostentatious disrespect toward the United States. Trump announced the truce on October 11. Ukraine says it has stopped hitting Russian refineries since. The Kremlin never confirmed a deal. It says only that contacts continue."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Zelenskyy says Kyiv got no early warning from partners. CNN reports Washington warned it could suspend intelligence sharing if Ukraine keeps striking Russian energy sites. Zelenskyy is asking for more Patriot interceptors."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will both sides stop hitting energy sites this winter? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
