  "title": "600,000 Without Power: Was the Energy Truce Real? #shorts",
  "description": "Ukraine says Russia fired 39 ballistic missiles and more than 120 drones at energy sites in Kyiv, the Kyiv region and Kharkiv overnight on October 13-14, leaving about 600,000 people without power. Zelenskyy calls it \"ostentatious disrespect\" toward the US after Trump announced an energy ceasefire on October 11. The Kremlin has not confirmed any truce; casualty figures differ between outlets and are Ukrainian claims.\n\nSources:\nAl Jazeera: 'Massive' Russian attack on Ukraine kills at least 9, damages power sites (Oct 14, 2026)\nCNN: Russia batters Ukraine's energy facilities hours after Zelensky appeals for early warnings from partners (Oct 14, 2026)\nPBS NewsHour / AP: Zelenskyy says Russia keeps striking Ukraine's energy sites despite Trump ceasefire push (Oct 14, 2026)\nThe Kyiv Independent: 'Ostentatious disrespect' - Zelensky says Russia defied Trump's energy ceasefire (Oct 14, 2026)\n\n#geopolitics #Ukraine #Russia #Ceasefire",
